## STEP 1 — DELTA

- [NEW] sdk: both `@gladiaio/sdk` (JS `client.ts`) and `gladiaio-sdk` (Py `client.py`) forward `audio_url` **verbatim** to `POST /v2/pre-recorded` — zero host/scheme/IP validation in `create`/`createUntyped`; the `is_url()` http/https check only gates the `uploadFile` convenience shortcut
- [NEW] api.gladia.io: OpenAPI `InitTranscriptionRequest.audio_url` = *"URL to a Gladia file or to an external audio or video file"* — server-side fetch of user-supplied external URLs is a **designed feature**, so SSRF exploitability reduces to blocklist quality
- [NEW] api.gladia.io: two legacy multipart endpoints `POST /audio/text/audio-transcription` and `POST /video/text/video-transcription` accept `audio_url`/`video_url` (default example `https://files.gladia.io/...`), key-gated per spec — second, possibly less-hardened outbound-fetch path
- [NEW] api.gladia.io: `callback_config.url` / deprecated `callback_url` — server does a `POST` to an attacker-supplied URL (second designed outbound-fetch surface)
- [NEW] api.gladia.io: unauthenticated `GET /v1/history` → 401 with NestJS-shaped body (`statusCode/timestamp/path` + `request_id G-...`) — distinct error shape vs v2 gate → legacy service behind `/v1/*` and `/audio|video/*`
- [NEW] api.gladia.io: `AudioUploadResponse.audio_url` example reveals stored-file scheme `https://api.gladia.io/file/<uuid>` (spec-only)
- [NEW] api.gladia.io: `/health?full=true` returns bare `{"health":"OK"}` — no verbose/runtime leak; queued probe closed

## STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE

- [PRIO] api.gladia.io /v2/pre-recorded audio_url SSRF — score 6.35 (attack 7 business 8 tech 6 gate 2 cloud 8 fresh 6)
- [PRIO] api.gladia.io legacy /audio//video/* endpoints — score 5.30 (attack 6 business 5 tech 5 gate 2 cloud 7 fresh 8)
- [PRIO] sdk npm `gladia` impersonation — score 5.20 (attack 4 business 6 tech 4 gate 10 cloud 2 fresh 4)
- [PRIO] app.gladia.io redirect_to OAuth — score 4.85 (attack 5 business 6 tech 6 gate 4 cloud 1 fresh 5)

## STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES

[HYP] SSRF via audio_url/video_url server-side fetch
class: SSRF
asset: api.gladia.io /v2/pre-recorded, /v2/upload, legacy /audio/text/audio-transcription + /video/text/video-transcription (audio_url/video_url)
confidence: 70
reasoning: SDK RAG confirms zero client-side validation (audio_url forwarded verbatim; is_url check only in uploadFile helper); OpenAPI spec confirms external-URL fetch is by design; legacy /audio|/video/* endpoints add a second fetch path with NestJS-shaped legacy service; /v1/models proves unauthenticated responses exist, so key-gated fetch logic is real.
evidence_needed: fetch of 169.254.169.254 or internal host reflected via error text/timing/job status on a key-gated request.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED — with a valid x-gladia-key: (1) POST /v2/pre-recorded `{"audio_url":"http://<attacker-canary>"}` → observe job error_code/timing; (2) same with `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/`; (3) repeat via /video/text/video-transcription `video_url` to compare legacy-path behavior; compare error/duration for reachability signal.
impact: cloud-metadata + internal-network read from API origin → High (key-gated)
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] Post-auth open redirect via redirect_to
class: OATH
asset: app.gladia.io /signin?redirect_to=
confidence: 55
reasoning: redirect_to reflected server-side into form action (verified GET); applies to both email/password and Google OAuth paths; unsigned return-to cookie proves server-driven redirect concept; only post-auth final Location unobserved.
evidence_needed: with a real session, final Location for cross-origin redirect_to (https://evil.example.com, //evil.example.com, https://evil.example.com.evil.io).
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED — complete sign-in (session), submit intent=email-password|google with redirect_to variants, capture post-auth Location and cookie set; escalate only if redirect_to is reused as OAuth redirect_uri.
impact: phishing / OAuth-flow manipulation → Low-Med (High only if redirect_uri injection proven)
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] Impersonation/name-squat `gladia` npm package
class: OTHER
asset: npm registry `gladia` 0.1.3 (dist-tag latest)
confidence: 78
reasoning: registry description "Official TypeScript SDK" vs packaged README "Unofficial"; maintainer softwarecitadel (personal gmail), repo alexisbouchez/gladia.ts, published 2025-03-28 before @gladiaio/sdk (2025-09-09); tarball benign (baseUrl api.gladia.io only).
evidence_needed: none — metadata verified; report as supply-chain hygiene/impersonation (Medium)
verify_steps: PASSIVE — already done (registry metadata + tarball inspection); document description-vs-README contradiction, maintainer mismatch, publish-date ordering
impact: developers installing `gladia` get unofficial code; account/repo hijack later → supply-chain compromise; Medium
testability: PASSIVE

## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE

- [PARKED] CORS wildcard (aggregated [65]): re-confirmed dead — no `access-control-allow-credentials`, cross-origin JS cannot carry x-gladia-key; no exploitable cross-origin read
- [PARKED] legacy /audio|/video endpoints as standalone hypothesis: merged into H1 — same class/gateway, no evidence yet that path is independently weaker
- [PARKED] /health runtime leak: probed `?full=true` — bare `{"health":"OK"}`, no verbose output; remains low-severity accepted MISCONFIG, no escalation
- [PARKED] OpenAPI shadow-endpoint enumeration: stays parked (active fuzzing prohibited under passive-first)
- [FINAL] ranked: 1) H1 SSRF @ api.gladia.io (70, SDK+spec-confirmed fetch surface) | 2) H3 npm impersonation (78, verified fact, PASSIVE) | 3) H2 open redirect @ app.gladia.io (55, needs session)

## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION

[NEXT] HUMAN: with a program-provided or personal trial `x-gladia-key`, POST https://api.gladia.io/v2/pre-recorded `{"audio_url":"http://<attacker-canary>"}` then `{"audio_url":"http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/"}`; compare job error_code/status/timing for reachability signal; then repeat via https://api.gladia.io/video/text/video-transcription `video_url` to test the legacy fetch path.

## STEP 6 — LEARNING

- [LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ api.gladia.io: /health ignores `?full=true` — bare `{"health":"OK"}`, no runtime detail leak
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED SSRF @ api.gladia.io: audio_url/video_url server-side fetch confirmed as designed feature (spec + SDK) — class alive, but key-gated and dependent on internal/metadata blocklist
- [LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ api.gladia.io: CORS wildcard re-confirmed non-exploitable (no allow-credentials; x-gladia-key can't be sent cross-origin)
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED AUTH @ api.gladia.io: /v1/history key-gated; NestJS-shaped 401 confirms legacy service behind /v1/* and /audio|/video/*

## STEP 7 — RISK SCORE

- [RISK] api.gladia.io: 48 | SSRF fetch surface confirmed as designed + key-gated, legacy /audio|/video/* adds second fetch path, uniform key gate, CORS * without credentials (low), public OpenAPI + bare /health leak minor
- [RISK] app.gladia.io: 40 | Google-only OAuth, reachable redirect_to with unvalidated post-auth behavior (unproven), cookies correctly flagged (HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax)
- [RISK] sdk: 50 | `gladia` npm package actively claims "Official" while unofficial (impersonation active); official @gladiaio/sdk metadata clean; `gladia` tarball benign so far
